; The high band added to the 48 kHz speech. Per sample in: the sample's thousands and units, as fir2 puts them
; out, and y from hfilt (the host deals 245 blank cards first, the 48 kHz speech's delay behind the 8 kHz speech).
; Out the sample plus 4 y, as its thousands and its units from 0 to 999: 4 y and the units summed on top of 4000, so
; that they never go negative, STO keeping the new units and SFT 03 giving the carry, as fir2 does.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            smp     INP   th       03-24: a sample, + 4 y
  04                    INP   u
  05                    INP   y
  06                    CLA   four
  07                    SFT   30
  08                    ADD   y
  09                    ADD   y
  10                    ADD   y
  11                    ADD   y
  12                    ADD   u
  13                    STO   u
  14                    SFT   03
  15                    ADD   th
  16                    SUB   four
  17                    STO   th
  18                    OUT   th
  19                    OUT   u
  20                    JMP   smp
  21            th      DATA  0
  22            u       DATA  0
  23            y       DATA  0
  24            four    DATA  4
